{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. I understand you came in with abdominal pain and neck swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. The pain in my belly is like my past Crohn’s flares. And my neck felt so tight, like I was wearing a turtleneck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Given your history, we’re concerned about a flare-up. We’ve placed a nasogastric tube to help decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s uncomfortable, but I know it helps. I’ve had this before. I just worry you’ll think I’m only here for pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe you. Your symptoms are real. We’re treating this as a Crohn’s flare. We’ve started IV fluids and antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My veins are bad though—always hard to get access. I had a femoral line tried in the ER but it failed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. A specialist placed a central line in your right neck under ultrasound guidance. It’s in the internal jugular."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was it safe? I have SVC syndrome—veins are narrow. I had angioplasty before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. The line is in, but we’ll monitor. We’re avoiding heparin because of your HIT history—using saline flushes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that. And the neck swelling—is it related to my veins?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-12-22 03:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’re ordering an MRV to check your SVC and neck veins. We want to rule out a clot or worsening blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-12-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your abdominal X-ray shows some distention but no clear obstruction. Bowel sounds are slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-12-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not a full blockage? That’s good. But the pain is still bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-12-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No obstruction on CT either. We think it’s inflammation from Crohn’s. You’re on IV Dilaudid for pain and ciprofloxacin for infection risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-12-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your MRV is back. It shows complete chronic occlusion of your SVC and both brachiocephalic veins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-12-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is that why my face swelled? Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-12-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that likely caused the swelling. But you’ve developed good collateral veins—alternate pathways. Vascular surgery says no procedure needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-12-25 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s stable? I’m relieved. But what about my line in the neck?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-12-25 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching it. Given your vein issues, we may need to move it later if it stops working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-12-26 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your current neck line is leaking from one port. We’re going to exchange it over the wire to a new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-12-26 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I need sedation. I get very anxious with procedures, especially with men around."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-12-26 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ll use Versed and fentanyl, and ensure female staff are present. Your comfort is important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-12-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The line exchange was successful. The new one is in the distal SVC. But your abdominal X-ray shows worsening obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-12-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel bloated. Is this going to turn into a full blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-12-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing it with the NG tube and bowel rest. Surgery doesn’t recommend surgery now. We’re hopeful it will improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-12-28 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a fever last night. My neck line site is red."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-12-28 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you spiked a fever to 103.8. There’s redness at the site. We’re starting Vancomycin for a possible line infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-12-28 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the line is working, right? I need it for meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-12-28 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It infuses, but we can’t draw blood from it. That’s concerning. We plan to move it tomorrow under sedation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-12-29 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tried to place a new line on the left side, but the veins are blocked. We had to re-site on the right neck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-12-29 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it working now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-12-29 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only one port draws blood. The others may be clotted. A chest X-ray suggests it might be in a collateral vein. We may need another change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-12-29 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve moved the line to your right groin. The neck line wasn’t functional. This femoral line is working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-12-29 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "In my leg? That’s new. Is it safe long-term?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-12-29 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. We’ll switch to a tunneled line later so you can go home on antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-12-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still anxious. Can I have something for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-12-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve lowered your diazepam dose because you were very sleepy. We can give oxazepam instead—less sedating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2187-01-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures and line tip were negative, but we’re continuing Vancomycin for 14 days due to high suspicion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2187-01-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I feel better. Fever’s gone. Can’t I stop early?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2187-01-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’d like you to finish. We’re placing a tunneled femoral line so you can get IV antibiotics at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2187-01-03 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We placed a tunneled line in your right groin. The left side was blocked. This one should stay secure for your Vancomycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2187-01-03 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. How long do I need it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2187-01-03 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fourteen days total. You’ve had nine so far. But we’ll monitor—your counts are low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2187-01-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your tunneled line came out accidentally. It’s no longer in the tunnel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2187-01-05 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no! Does that mean I have to stay longer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2187-01-05 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been fever-free for 48 hours and have had nine days of antibiotics. We discussed with you—discharge is safe with close follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2187-01-05 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about infection coming back. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2187-01-05 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fever, chills, redness at any site. Come back immediately if that happens. You’ll get blood tests and cultures in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2187-01-05 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your abdominal pain has improved. You’re passing gas and tolerating soft foods. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2187-01-05 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad. I was scared it would turn into a full obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2187-01-05 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tethering from scar tissue is still there, but not blocking. We’ll keep you on ciprofloxacin and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2187-01-05 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my anemia? My ferritin was low before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2187-01-05 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is low at 8.6. We’ll follow up with your PCP. Iron deficiency is likely, given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. You’re doing much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. But what about pain at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get Dilaudid 4 mg—take one every three hours as needed. Don’t hesitate to use it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And for anxiety?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Oxazepam 15 mg twice daily as needed. We’re also restarting your citalopram."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m worried about future hospital stays. It’s so hard with my veins and anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We recommend a team meeting before any future admission—doctors, nurses, social work—to plan together with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would help so much. Thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2187-01-06 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send all instructions and prescriptions. Follow up with GI, vascular, and your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2187-01-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re removing the femoral line since it’s no longer tunneled. You’ll go home without a line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2187-01-06 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll watch for any signs of infection and come back if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2187-01-06 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’ve done well. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-12-22 02:50:00",
    "admission_end": "2187-01-06 15:03:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a complex history of Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, SVC syndrome, and multiple prior surgeries was admitted with a Crohn’s flare, abdominal pain, and facial swelling. Imaging showed no bowel obstruction but revealed chronic complete occlusion of the SVC and brachiocephalic veins with collateralization, explaining her neck swelling. She developed a suspected central line infection in her right internal jugular catheter, presenting with fever and erythema, and was treated with intravenous Vancomycin. Due to non-functional lines and venous thrombosis, she required multiple central line revisions, ultimately receiving a femoral tunneled line for outpatient antibiotic therapy, which dislodged before discharge. Her abdominal symptoms improved with bowel rest, NG decompression, and pain management. She was discharged home after nine days of antibiotics, afebrile, with improved pain control, and a plan for close outpatient follow-up, including blood work and monitoring for infection recurrence.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine",
      "Suspected RIJ Central Line infection",
      "Acute on Chronic SVC Syndrome",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Paralytic ileus",
      "Chronic venous embolism and thrombosis of other thoracic veins",
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Dehydration"
    ]
  }
}
